## What

Stage 4, item 3: **whole sites bound to real data, one per field.** A new page under ميزاتي, «مواقع كاملة» (`/admin/my-features/sites`), lists 12 sites:

| Field | Sites |
|---|---|
| Food and drink | restaurant, bakery and café |
| Health | dental clinic |
| Beauty | beauty salon |
| Fitness | gym |
| Learning | course centre |
| Property and stays | real-estate office, guest house |
| Events | events hall |
| Creative | photographer |
| Services | law office, creative agency |

Each one is a feature template (`.feature.json`). It is shown before anything is written, installed as a draft, upgraded and removed like any template.

## What a site holds

- **Pages (6 or 7):**
  - built from the existing section library (openings, stories, pictures, calls, contact), in the site's own words, in one of six compositions;
  - the first page, the main list (menu, treatments, classes, listings…) with one section per group, our story with the team, news, questions, contact, and booking where the field has one.
- **8 tables with about 24 ready rows**, in ar/en/he:
  - the main list (price, group, picture, "on the first page"), team, reviews, questions, news and branches;
  - the pages' lists read these tables: change a row and the site follows;
  - the main list and the news have a page per row (`/dishes/hummus`).
- **Forms that write into the site's own tables:** messages and booking requests. Visitors can add rows; nobody reads them but the store.
- **A function** that rings the owner's bell for each message or booking. It is a draft until published.
- **The store's own home stays as it is.** The site's first page has its own address (`/restaurant`).

## Changes beneath it

- **Ready rows in the template format** (`tables[].rows`, up to 60 a table):
  - checked as the data grid checks a row: field kinds, rules and defaults;
  - every problem is reported where it is: a field the table doesn't have, a link to rows, a doubled address, a doubled value in a field that holds one of each;
  - an upgrade adds rows only to a table it makes new;
  - export never writes a store's rows.
- **A list drawn with the page now honours its filters** (`rowMatches`), e.g. "only the starters" or "only the ones on the first page". Before, only lists read in the browser did. The editor's list panel now shows filters for every list.
- **Fix: a table's row pages stayed on the shop when its feature was switched off.** They now answer 404, so a site installed as a draft really is a draft.
- **Fix: a list drawn with a page kept showing old rows for up to 5 minutes after a row changed.** The server's cached page answer was renewed only when the page itself changed. `triggerCmsRevalidate`, which already runs after a row changes, now renews it too.

## Code

- **Admin:**
  - `studio/templates/sites/`: `siteKit.ts` (the builder: the library's sections plus the data sections whose cards are connected to fields) and four content files;
  - `features/myFeatures/SitesPage.tsx` and `sitesText.ts`;
  - the preview shows each table's ready rows;
  - `FeatureUpgrade` also offers a newer version of a site, built in the admin;
  - the list panel's filters.
- **Backend:**
  - `lib/featureTemplate.ts` (rows), `lib/featureInstall.ts`, `lib/collectionTree.ts` (`rowMatches`);
  - `lib/cmsRevalidate.ts`;
  - `modules/storefront/storefront.routes.ts`.
- Docs: the T section of the backend plan and stage 4 of the full-stack plan.
- No migration.

## Checked

- **Backend:**
  - typecheck;
  - `siteTemplates.unit.spec.ts`:
    - every site in every language and both motion levels reads as a template and plans its install with no problem;
    - its lists name its own tables, and its forms and buttons go to its own tables and pages;
    - ready rows are checked;
    - `rowMatches` is tested.
  - `sites.spec.ts` (database):
    - all 12 install beside each other with their rows;
    - the home's featured lists and the main page's group lists are filled with exactly the right rows;
    - nothing shows on the shop while the feature is off (pages, row pages, the messages table);
    - once on: the page shows, a cached page follows a changed row (this check fails without the cache fix), a dish's page shows, and a message lands in its table;
    - a second site's shared addresses move and its forms and links follow;
    - everything leaves without a trace.
  - The whole suite (1,399 passed; only `pages.publishing` and `visualControls.integration`, as always locally). Two publication-delivery unit tests needed the cache stand-in to have the new call.
- **Admin:** typecheck; `sites.test.tsx` and one more upgrade test; the whole suite (1,480); the build.
- **A real run on this PC** (local server on the throwaway database, the admin's real sites page, a local shop on the same server):
  - the restaurant was picked, its preview showed "8 ready rows", and it installed with 7 draft pages;
  - the shop answered 404 while it was off;
  - once switched on and published, the home, the menu (grouped), the contact page and a dish's page showed;
  - the phone width had no sideways scroll;
  - a changed row reached the page;
  - the real contact form wrote its message into the messages table.
  - Found and fixed in that run: the cache gap above, a phone line that read backwards in Arabic, sample shop hours on the contact page, and the first page's name.

