## What this does

**My Clique** is every creator a member follows. It is `social.follows`, unchanged and still the source of truth, with no limit. **Inner Clique** is an optional priority group of up to 25 followed creators, kept in the existing `social.clique_members`. There are no new tables, and every existing follow and membership is preserved.

### Migration `20261120000000_inner_clique.sql` (staging only)
* The guard trigger now allows 25 open memberships, and still requires a follow.
* New `app_clique_replace(p_remove, p_add)` swaps one creator for another in a single transaction, under the existing per-member advisory lock. If any check fails, nothing changes. The replaced creator stays followed, and their row is closed as `replaced`.
* `app_unfollow` now takes the same lock, so it can't race an add or a replace and leave a membership without a follow. Otherwise its behaviour is unchanged.
* `removal_reason` now also allows `replaced`.
* **Rate limit:** the existing `social.rate_check(text, uuid)` keeps its signature and allows 120 Inner Clique changes per rolling hour per member.
  * Add and remove pass kind `clique`, which counts as one change. Replace passes `clique_replace`, which counts as two.
  * A request is refused when the existing changes plus its own would go past 120. So a replacement at 118 is allowed (reaching 120) and at 119 it is refused, while a single add at 119 is still allowed.
  * Posts, comments and follows count as one change each, so they behave exactly as before.
  * Requests that change nothing aren't counted, and a refused request (`rate_limited`) changes nothing.
  * Unfollow stays under the follow limit.
  * A new index, `clique_by_fan_recent`, keeps the count cheap.
* Same security model as before: security definer, empty search_path, signed-in members only (anon and public revoked).
* Not in `supabase/production-migrations.txt`.
* **Checksum approved by the founder:** `cab49c99010aff1d8dd90bf4c8f8c5d66dd25869877a689e1e66a4e79032dabf`. It was added to `supabase/approved-migrations.sha256` in its own commit, `b4025bf`. All 9 migrations are approved and unchanged.

### App
The existing Clique tab now has two sections. There's no new tab.
* **Inner Clique:** a count (for example 8/25) and "Remove from Inner Clique", which never unfollows.
* **My Clique:** every followed creator with their status, plus "Add to Inner Clique" and "Unfollow". Unfollowing also removes the creator from the Inner Clique.
* **When full:** at 25, adding opens a replacement dialog built on the existing `Modal`, which is a bottom sheet on phones. It has a labelled radio group and explains that the replaced creator stays in My Clique. Escape and Cancel close it, focus is trapped inside it, and focus returns to the button afterwards.
* **After a failed or stale replacement:**
  * the dialog stays open, shows the error and moves focus to it;
  * the list refreshes, and the chosen creator stays selected while they're still in the Inner Clique;
  * if a place opened up elsewhere, the dialog offers a plain add;
  * if the creator was already added or unfollowed elsewhere, the dialog says so.
* **Elsewhere:** on profiles and Discover, a full Inner Clique shows "Choose who to replace", which links to `/app/clique?add=<id>`.

### Rollback (staging only)
`scripts/db/staging-rollback-inner-clique.sql` restores the earlier definitions byte for byte:
* the guard at 10;
* `app_unfollow`, `app_clique_add`, `app_clique_remove` and `social.rate_check`;
* the removal reasons and the comments.

It also drops the replace function and the new index, and deletes the migration record.

It refuses, changing nothing, if:
* any member has more than 10 Inner Clique creators;
* any membership was closed as `replaced`;
* a later migration is recorded.

**Accepted:** once members use the 25-creator capacity, problems are fixed forward rather than rolled back. It is wired first into `scripts/db/rollback-test.sh`, ahead of the other rollbacks.

## Tests
* `supabase/tests-local/066_inner_clique.sql`:
  * unlimited follows (29), and the 25 cap with the 26th refused;
  * replace works, and the replaced creator stays followed;
  * six kinds of failed replace that change nothing, plus one forced to fail at its last step that also changes nothing;
  * remove keeps the follow, and unfollow closes the membership;
  * anonymous visitors are refused, and other members are unaffected;
  * **rate limit:** refused add, remove and replace write nothing;
  * requests that change nothing are not counted;
  * follow and unfollow keep working while the member is limited;
  * the one-hour window;
  * **the boundary:** at 118, a replacement is allowed and the count reaches 120;
  * at 119, a replacement is refused with memberships and history unchanged, while a single add is still allowed;
  * the follow limit is unchanged (the 120th change allowed, the 121st refused);
  * no points, rewards or ranking, and the feed stays chronological.
  * The 119 test fails against the old `n >= v_limit` check (verified).
* `supabase/tests/005_social_core.sql`: staging-safe checks that add and remove use `clique`, replace uses `clique_replace`, and the check is cost-aware.
* `scripts/db/inner-clique-concurrency-test.sh` uses two real sessions:
  * the same creator replaced twice;
  * two different replacements;
  * the same creator brought in twice;
  * an add racing a replace at 25;
  * unfollow and replace racing, in both orders;
  * **two replacements at once at 118 changes:** one applies (reaching 120) and the other is refused.
* `scripts/db/rollback-inner-clique-test.sh`: 14 checks. These include the restored rate limit functions and index, and applying the migration over existing open and closed memberships with all of them kept.
* `src/app/app.test.tsx`:
  * the page, the dialog, and the keyboard (Escape, Cancel, focus restore);
  * a refused replacement that keeps the choice, focuses the error and can be retried;
  * a stale choice that is refreshed, followed by a successful second choice;
  * a place opening up elsewhere;
  * an unfollow elsewhere;
  * the `?add=` link.
* `e2e/social-journey.e2e.cjs`:
  * 27 follows, with the 26th Inner Clique add refused;
  * anonymous replace refused;
  * a real replacement in the browser;
  * a stale replacement made from another device while the dialog is open;
  * remove without unfollowing, and follow and unfollow;
  * no sideways scroll at 390 and 320 px.

